#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation.rst:63
msgid "Which install should you choose?"
msgstr "您應該選擇哪一種安裝？"

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation.rst:65
msgid ""
"Installing from binary packages or from source will both result in a fully-"
"functional and usable ROS 2 install. Differences between the options depend "
"on what you plan to do with ROS 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation.rst:68
msgid ""
"**Binary packages** are for general use and provide an already-built install "
"of ROS 2. This is great for people who want to dive in and start using ROS 2 "
"as-is, right away."
msgstr ""
"**二進位軟體包**\\ 適合一般使用者，提供已經建置完成的 ROS 2 安裝。這對於想要"
"立即開始使用 ROS 2 的人來說非常方便。"

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation.rst:71
msgid "Linux users have two options for installing binary packages:"
msgstr "Linux 使用者有兩種安裝二進位軟體包的選項："

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation.rst:73
msgid "Packages (debs or RPMS, depending on the platform)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation.rst:74
msgid "binary archive"
msgstr "二進位封存檔"

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation.rst:76
msgid ""
"Installing from packages is the recommended method, as it installs necessary "
"dependencies automatically and also updates alongside regular system "
"updates. However, you need root access in order to install deb packages. If "
"you don't have root access, the binary archive is the next best choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation.rst:80
msgid ""
"Windows users who choose to install from binary packages only have the "
"binary archive option (deb packages are exclusive to Ubuntu/Debian)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation.rst:83
msgid ""
"**Building from source** is meant for developers looking to alter or "
"explicitly omit parts of ROS 2's base. It is also recommended for platforms "
"that don't support binaries. Building from source also gives you the option "
"to install the absolute latest version of ROS 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation.rst:88
msgid "Contributing to ROS 2 core?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation.rst:90
msgid ""
"If you plan to contribute directly to ROS 2 core packages, you can install "
"the :doc:`latest development from source <Installation/Alternatives/Latest-"
"Development-Setup>` which shares installation instructions with the :ref:"
"`Rolling distribution <rolling_distribution>`."
msgstr ""
